  "_about": "News sources the daily run reads, chosen for a Boston-based US reader (owner request, 2026-10-25): major US national outlets first, Boston/New England outlets for local news, and a few international outlets mainly for corroboration. 'group' = independence group: two sources in the same group never count as independent corroboration. 'region' = us | boston | intl. 'front' = true for an outlet's top-stories/home-page feed, which is a signal of what that outlet is leading with. 'kind': news = original reporting; press = press releases / primary source. Checked on 2026-10-25. Left out: AP (403 forbidden), Boston Herald (403), USA Today (402 payment required), Washington Post (502), GBH (no working feed), CNN and WSJ (stale feeds), and France 24 (bot check).",
